# .gitignore — skill-opinion-to-ruler

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Runtime landing spot for regenerated products — a *product*, never the anchor.
# `evaluate.py` rewrites this directory on every run, so it is machine-local and
# must stay out of the package.
output/

# The acceptance anchor ships with the skill: baselines/frozen_baseline.json and
# baselines/scope_declaration.json are the frozen reference the specification
# demands (「冻结基线对照」). An anchor living inside a git-ignored directory does
# not exist for anyone installing from git, so this negation is load-bearing:
# it keeps the anchor tracked even if a broad `*.json` rule is added later.
# It is deliberately scoped to baselines/ — do NOT widen it to `!output/*`, which
# would put regenerated products back into the package and let two copies each
# claim to be authoritative.
!baselines/*.json

# Agent-landed PandaData MCP payloads: verbatim tool responses, machine-local and
# reproducible by re-running the fetch. Never committed.
tests/fixtures/raw/*
!tests/fixtures/raw/README.md

# Bars built from those payloads by scripts/mcp_landing.py --build. Also
# reproducible, and real market data does not belong in a repo.
tests/fixtures/landed/*
!tests/fixtures/landed/README.md

# NOTE: tests/fixtures/*.csv at the top level (bars_RB.csv, bars_I.csv) are the
# bundled *synthetic* fixtures the docs and the offline tests depend on. They stay
# committed, and landed real data is deliberately written to a different directory
# so a real run can never silently shadow a fixture run.
